ovum-studies-ledger change log: why each change was made, newest first.

2026-11-10  v1r's results
  WHY: v1r ran after its registration (record 31), on the Central Compiler, and every figure it prints matched v1's
  2026-10-05 record. Its results are entered so that a reader can check them against the registration.
  - ledger.tsv, records 32 to 34: one per run and its receipt, each the SHA-256 of the results as committed in the lab's
    repository at 3a88029f894d, which is that repository's published main.

2026-11-10  v1r registered before it runs
  WHY: the operator ruled on 2026-11-09 that v1 is rerun before Ovum 1.0, as a pre-registered reproduction of its
  2026-10-05 runs. The reproduction is registered here before any run, so its own registration has the contract's form.
  - ledger.tsv, record 31: the SHA-256 of v1r's pre-registration as committed in the lab's repository at 2734373880b2,
    which is that repository's published main.

2026-11-10  The 30 capability studies, backfilled
  WHY: the 30 studies behind Ovum's capabilities were registered before this ledger existed, in Ovum's own history,
  before they moved to the lab on 2026-10-31. Their records are entered now, marked backfill-registration, so a reader
  can see that their proof of time rests on Ovum's history and not on this ledger.
  - ledger.tsv, records 1 to 30, in order of birth: each is the SHA-256 of the pre-registration's bytes at its birth
    commit on Ovum's main branch, and that commit.
  - Checked before writing: all 30 birth commits equal those Ovum's own release checker (deploy/check-custody.sh) found
    independently, each is an ancestor of Ovum's main branch as GitHub reported it (5f27b0ca), and each digest was
    recomputed from the bytes. Custody-daemon snapshot commits, which are not on main, were excluded.

2026-11-09  The ledger is made
  WHY: for studies, git history pushed to GitHub is the custody ledger (operator ruling, 2026-11-09). A separate public
  repository of digests makes that history public and protected, without revealing any study. The operator created the
  repository, its deploy key and its main ruleset (no deletion, no force-push, no bypass).
  - README.md: what the ledger proves and does not, the record format and the rules.
  - ledger.tsv: the schema and the header, with no records yet. The 30 existing capability studies follow as backfill.
